  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shepherd's pie uses minced lamb rather than beef, which gives it a stronger flavour and a slightly looser texture under the mash. Rosemary is the herb that goes with lamb, and it makes all the difference here. The filling "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "simmers",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "simmering"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " until the gravy is thick and clings to the meat, then the mash goes on top and the whole thing bakes until golden."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
